    "question": "When should I use Docker containers instead of a virtual machine, and what is the real difference?",
    "summary": "Docker containers and virtual machines both provide isolated environments for running applications, but containers share the host OS kernel and are lightweight and fast, while VMs emulate full hardware and offer stronger isolation. The right choice depends on your requirements for isolation,…",
